# Repositories this machine plans for, one absolute path per line.
#
# Copy to repos.personal.conf (or repos.<profile>.conf for another machine).
# The copy is gitignored: it names your own repositories. Opting a repository
# in is a deliberate act: what it opts in to is an agent writing a branch
# there unattended, nightly, with nobody watching. An absent file means
# nothing participates, which is the right default for that.
#
# The path must be one the `repo` table already holds — `sd-db.sh repo list`
# is the enumeration. A path here that is not registered is a line that names
# nothing, and `nightly` says so rather than skipping it quietly.

# /Users/<you>/repos/system-tools
